Implemented a fix in the Excel parsing logic to correctly handle blank/empty cells during file processing. Previously, if a cell was blank, the parser skipped that position and shifted the subsequent cell values to the left, which caused incorrect column mapping and data mismatches in downstream processing.
With this enhancement, blank cells are now preserved while reading each row, ensuring that all column positions remain aligned with the original Excel structure. This guarantees accurate value mapping, prevents data displacement issues, and improves overall reliability of file processing.
